## Context

Paper trading week 1 (Mar 11-18, 2026) exposed catastrophic vulnerability in momentum strategies:
- BAN crash: -55% in 14h, cost s56 -$88K, s60 -$104K, s69 -$43K, s76 -$29K across portfolios
- PIPPIN crash: -70% over 6 days, repeated LONG re-entries as token declined
- Total damage: $265K from 4 momentum strategies (89% of all BAN/PIPPIN losses)
- Carry/mean-rev strategies (s59, s62, s72) PROFITED from the same events by shorting

Root cause: s56's entry conditions (strong uptrend, BB breakout, volume explosion, high ADX)
are the EXACT signature of a pump-and-dump's pump phase. s60 inherits this on LONG side.
CB was A/B tested per-strategy and genuinely hurts momentum strategies (doubles MaxDD).
The fix must be entry-side, not exit-side.

## Improvement Stack (priority order)

### P1: ADV-Scaled Position Sizing (sizing.py)
- sqrt(ADV / $100M) scaling, clamped [0.15, 1.0]
- BAN ($17M ADV): 0.41x sizing → $5.3K vs current $13K
- 3 files: sizing.py, config.py, simulator.py
- No strategy changes needed

### P2: Drawdown-from-Recent-High Filter (simulator entry filter)
- Block LONG when price >30% below 7-day rolling high
- dd_7d = (close - rolling_max(close, 168)) / rolling_max(close, 168)
- Block if dd_7d < threshold (e.g., -0.30)
- New StrategySpec fields: drawdown_filter_window, drawdown_filter_threshold
- Would have blocked all PIPPIN entries below $0.28

### P3: Smart Volatility Regime Filter (strategy or simulator level)
- Distinguish GOOD vol (volume leads price = accumulation) from BAD vol (price extended + vol chase)
- 4 components: ATR expansion rate, volume-price sequencing, range/ATR exhaustion, OBV divergence
- Good vol overrides block (genuine breakout allowed)
- More complex — may implement as strategy-level overlay

### P4: Post-Pump Cooldown
- After >20% move in 24h, block entries for 48h cooldown
- Detects pump-then-dump pattern
- New StrategySpec fields: pump_cooldown_threshold, pump_cooldown_bars

### P5: Token Loss Memory / Re-entry Cooldown
- Track last N closed trades per token per strategy
- Block if 3+ of last 5 trades were losses, or halve size if avg PnL negative
- Requires runtime state in SimulationState
- Paper engine only initially (biased in backtesting)

### P6: Anti-Signal Patterns (additional filters for later)
- Funding-price divergence (funding positive + price declining = long squeeze coming)
- ADV decline detector (24h ADV < 50% of 7d ADV = liquidity withdrawal)
- Regime crash velocity (UPTREND→DOWNTREND in 12 bars = panic cooldown)
- Secular decline detector (MTF: daily EMA20 < EMA50 + 4h close < EMA20)

